rows.answer:
A qualified adviser will contact you. The switchboard number is 0117 496 0100.

If a client has died, the documents say to let us know as soon as you are able. You can also use the Death Notification Service, which tells several financial firms at once. We will need:
- the original or a certified copy of the death certificate;
- details of the executors or administrators of the estate;
- the grant of probate or letters of administration (in Scotland, Confirmation) before assets can be released.

Where the total value held with us is below £30,000, we can usually release assets to the personal representatives without a grant, against a signed indemnity.

